# Operational Rules for Cline

## 1. API RATE LIMIT & COOLING

- In case of 429 (Resource Exhausted) or 503 errors, automatically pause for 60 seconds before retrying.
- Group file reads to minimize consecutive API calls.
- Maintain a 2 to 3-second gap between autonomous actions to avoid saturating the Requests Per Minute (RPM) limit.

### Automated Error Handling (429 / 503)

- If an API response returns 429 (Resource Exhausted) or 503 (Service Unavailable):
  1. Parse the error and identify if it is a daily quota issue or rate-limit peak.
  2. Immediately instruct the user: "Se agotó la cuota o hubo un error con el modelo [modelo]. Por favor, selecciona un modelo alternativo en la configuración de OpenRouter o intenta nuevamente en unos momentos."
  3. Pause operations until the user switches models or confirms retrying.

## 2. TERMINAL SYNTAX (POWERSHELL)

- This environment uses Windows PowerShell 5.1.
- NEVER use the `&&` operator to chain commands. Use `;` or separate commands instead.

## 3. REPOSITORY SECURITY

- Keep changes small and iterative.
- Do not modify or delete legacy files or backup databases.
- Always confirm the active Git branch before editing code.
